The '''[[2019–20 in Scottish football|2019–20 season]]''' was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 131st season of competitive football. They competed in the [[2019–20 Scottish Premiership|Scottish Premiership]], [[2019–20 Scottish Cup|Scottish Cup]], [[2019–20 Scottish League Cup|League Cup]], [[2019–20 UEFA Champions League|Champions League]] and [[2019–20 UEFA Europa League|Europa League]]. Celtic won all three domestic tournaments, completing an unprecedented [[Treble (association football)|quadruple treble]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2020/december/Celtic-make-history-with-Quadruple-Treble-triumph-at-Hampden/ | title=Celtic make history with Quadruple Treble triumph at Hampden | publisher=Celtic FC | date=20 December 2020 | access-date=20 December 2020 | archive-date=20 December 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201220200404/https://www.celticfc.com/news/2020/december/Celtic-make-history-with-Quadruple-Treble-triumph-at-Hampden/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

On 13 March 2020, the Scottish football season was suspended with immediate effect due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://spfl.co.uk/news/coronavirus-joint-response-group-update-46618 | title=Coronavirus – Joint Response Group Update | publisher=SPFL | date=13 March 2020 | access-date=13 March 2020 | archive-date=19 March 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200319205638/https://spfl.co.uk/news/coronavirus-joint-response-group-update-46618 | url-status=live }}</ref> The season was curtailed as a result, with Celtic declared Scottish Premiership champions on 18 May, winning a [[Nine in a row|ninth consecutive league title]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/18108 | title=Champions again. This is our 9. | publisher=Celtic FC | date=18 May 2020 | access-date=18 May 2020 | archive-date=18 May 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200518161723/http://www.celticfc.net/news/18108 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/52706917 | title=Celtic: Neil Lennon targets 10 in row after his best achievement in football | publisher=BBC Sport | date=18 May 2020 | access-date=20 May 2020 | archive-date=2 December 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201202221045/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/52706917 | url-status=live }}</ref>

==Pre-season and friendlies==
Celtic held its pre-season training camp in [[Stegersbach]] (Austria) and [[St. Gallen]] (Switzerland), with matches against SC Pinkafeld, [[Wiener Sport-Club|Wiener SC]] and [[FC St. Gallen|St. Gallen]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16034 | title=Celtic announce pre-season training camp matches | publisher=Celtic FC | date=17 April 2019 | access-date=17 April 2019 | archive-date=17 April 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190417134348/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16034 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16233 | title=Celtic to play Stade Rennais in pre-season friendly at Paradise | publisher=Celtic FC | date=28 May 2019 | access-date=28 May 2019 | archive-date=28 May 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190528151902/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16233 | url-status=live }}</ref>

