==Scottish Cup==
{{Main|2019–20 Scottish Cup}}
On 24 November, Celtic were drawn to face [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] at [[Firhill Stadium]] in the fourth round of the [[2019–20 Scottish Cup]].<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50540633 | title=Scottish Cup: Celtic face Partick Thistle | publisher=BBC Sport | date=24 November 2019 | access-date=24 November 2019 | archive-date=24 November 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191124220512/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/50540633 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Scottish Cup holders progressed to the fifth round with a 2–1 victory. On 19 January 2020, Celtic were drawn to face [[Clyde F.C.|Clyde]] at [[Broadwood Stadium]] in the fifth round.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/17406 | title=Celtic to face Clyde in Scottish Cup fifth round | publisher=Celtic FC | date=19 January 2020 | access-date=19 January 2020 | archive-date=16 February 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200216124404/http://www.celticfc.net/news/17406 | url-status=live }}</ref> Goals from [[Olivier Ntcham]], [[Scott Brown (footballer, born June 1985)|Scott Brown]] and [[Vakoun Issouf Bayo]] sealed Celtic's place in the quarter-finals. On 9 February, Celtic were drawn to face [[St Johnstone F.C.|St Johnstone]] at [[McDiarmid Park]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/17515 | title=Celtic face away tie against St Johnstone in Scottish Cup last eight | publisher=Celtic FC | date=9 February 2020 | access-date=9 February 2020 | archive-date=11 September 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200911173948/http://www.celticfc.net/news/17515 | url-status=live }}</ref> A late [[Ryan Christie]] free-kick secured Celtic's place in the semi-finals. On 1 March, Celtic were drawn to face [[Aberdeen F.C.|Aberdeen]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/17623 | title=Celtic face Aberdeen in Scottish Cup semi-final at Hampden | publisher=Celtic FC | date=1 March 2020 | access-date=1 March 2020 | archive-date=1 March 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200301175029/http://www.celticfc.net/news/17623 | url-status=live }}</ref> As a result of the [[COVID-19 pandemic]] and subsequent suspension of Scottish football, the semi-finals were rescheduled for later in the year.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/53478993 | title=Scottish Cup: 2019-20 final scheduled for 20 December | publisher=BBC Sport | date=21 July 2020 | access-date=21 July 2020 | archive-date=21 July 2020 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200721141024/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/53478993 | url-status=live }}</ref>

