==Scottish League Cup==
{{Main|2019–20 Scottish League Cup}}
On 28 July, Celtic were drawn to face [[Dunfermline Athletic F.C.|Dunfermline Athletic]] at [[Celtic Park]] in the second round of the [[2019–20 Scottish League Cup]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16530 | title=Celtic take on Dunfermline Athletic at Paradise in League Cup | publisher=Celtic FC | date=28 July 2019 | access-date=28 July 2019 | archive-date=28 July 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190728222019/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16530 | url-status=live }}</ref> The League Cup holders progressed to the quarter-finals with a 2–1 victory in extra-time. On 18 August, Celtic were drawn to face [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] at [[Celtic Park]] in the quarter-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16667 | title=Celtic to play Partick Thistle in last eight of Betfred Cup | publisher=Celtic FC | date=18 August 2019 | access-date=18 August 2019 | archive-date=18 August 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190818175819/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16667 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys' trophy defence continued with a five-goal win against the [[Scottish Championship|Championship]] side. On 25 September, Celtic were drawn to face [[Hibernian F.C.|Hibernian]] in the semi-finals.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16857 | title=Celtic to face Hibernian in Betfred League Cup semi-final | publisher=[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] | date=25 September 2019 | access-date=8 November 2019 | archive-date=8 November 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191108161734/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16857 | url-status=live }}</ref> Goals from [[Mohamed Elyounoussi]], [[Callum McGregor]] and [[Scott Brown (footballer, born June 1985)|Scott Brown]] secured Celtic's place in the final, a fourth consecutive League Cup final and seventh consecutive domestic cup final. On 8 December, Celtic won the [[Scottish League Cup]] for the fourth consecutive season, defeating [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] [[2019–20 Scottish League Cup#Final|1–0]] in the [[2019 Scottish League Cup Final|final]].

