==UEFA Champions League==
{{Main|2019–20 UEFA Champions League}}
Celtic entered the Champions League at the first qualifying round.

===First qualifying round===
On 18 June, Celtic were drawn to face [[FK Sarajevo|Sarajevo]] ([[Bosnia and Herzegovina]]) in the first qualifying round of the [[2019–20 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16309 | title=Celtic face FK Sarajevo in UEFA Champions League | publisher=Celtic FC | date=18 June 2019 | access-date=18 June 2019 | archive-date=18 June 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190618130503/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16309 | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16321 | title=Celts travel away for opening leg against FK Sarajevo | publisher=Celtic FC | date=19 June 2019 | access-date=19 June 2019 | archive-date=19 June 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190619145729/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16321 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys won 5–2 on aggregate and secured a place in the next round.

