===Second qualifying round===
On 17 July, it was determined that Celtic would face [[Nõmme Kalju FC|Nõmme Kalju]] ([[Estonia]]) in the second qualifying round of the [[2019–20 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16464 | title=Celtic's Champions League journey continues with win over Sarajevo | publisher=Celtic FC | date=17 July 2019 | access-date=17 July 2019 | archive-date=17 July 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190717221134/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16464 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Scottish champions progressed to the third round with a 7–0 aggregate win against the Estonians.

