===Third qualifying round===
On 30 July, it was determined that Celtic would face [[CFR Cluj]] ([[Romania]]) in the third qualifying round of the [[2019–20 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16545 | title=Marian Shved hits debut goal as Celtic cruise to victory in Estonia | publisher=Celtic FC | date=30 July 2019 | access-date=30 July 2019 | archive-date=30 July 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190730191550/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16545 | url-status=live }}</ref> The Bhoys were eliminated following a 5–4 aggregate defeat and parachuted into the [[2019–20 UEFA Europa League qualifying phase and play-off round (Champions Path)|UEFA Europa League play-off round]].

