==UEFA Europa League==
{{Main|2019–20 UEFA Europa League}}

===Play-off round===
On 15 August, it was determined that Celtic would face [[AIK Fotboll|AIK]] (Sweden) in the play-off round of the [[2019–20 UEFA Europa League|UEFA Europa League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16656 | title=Celtic v AIK Europa League play-off tickets on sale now | publisher=Celtic FC | date=16 August 2019 | access-date=16 August 2019 | archive-date=16 August 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190816160145/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16656 | url-status=live }}</ref> [[Neil Lennon]]'s side recorded a comfortable 6–1 win on aggregate and secured a place in the [[2019–20 UEFA Europa League group stage]].

