*'''Home:''' The home kit features the club's traditional green and white hoops, with a green polo-style collar. White shorts and predominantly green socks complete the look.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16112 | title=New Balance reveals Celtic 2019/20 Home Kit | publisher=Celtic FC | date=1 May 2019 | access-date=1 June 2019 | archive-date=1 June 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190601142554/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16112 | url-status=live }}</ref>
*'''Away:''' The away kit features a lemon chrome shirt, with deep teal green shoulders. The shirt is accompanied by deep teal shorts and lemon chrome socks.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16336 | title=Celtic 2019/20 new balance away kit is officially revealed | publisher=Celtic FC | date=24 June 2019 | access-date=6 July 2019 | archive-date=6 July 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190706204025/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16336 | url-status=live }}</ref>
*'''Third:''' The third kit features a grey shirt, with a berry chevron on the front, a design that was first used on a Celtic shirt one hundred years before. Grey and berry shorts and socks complete the look.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.celticfc.net/news/16524 | title=Celtic 2019/20 New Balance Third Kit is officially revealed | publisher=Celtic FC | date=26 July 2019 | access-date=16 August 2019 | archive-date=16 August 2019 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190816160143/http://www.celticfc.net/news/16524 | url-status=live }}</ref>

